# Defect 216 (panel 188, 2026-10-03): a header's name holding what C11
# 6.4.7p3 leaves undefined between `<` and `>` (its text in the sitting's
# historian's report): `'`, `"`, `//` and `/*`. Clang reads each as itself and
# says nothing even under `-Weverything`, so without the rule the program has
# one compiler's meaning, which is why the code is a thesis rule
# (`diag.is_thesis_rule`). Until then `"` reached clang as its source
# spelling, two bytes, and `build` said the header was missing. The fifth
# mark, `\`, is refused apart (`fixedbugs-216-a-backslash-in-a-header-name`).
#
# The shape beside: an escape is decoded before it is judged, so `\t` is a
# control character (`unshowable_name`, stage D) and no longer a Windows root
# as the spelling's first byte made it.
#
# 2026-10-03, defect 235: `*` is refused in any name, no NTFS file holding
# one, and what nothing carries is told before a thesis rule (panel 188), so
# `e/*b.h` is `unwritable_name` now, its `/*` no longer reached.
#
# 2026-10-07, defect 445: `"` stands in no NTFS file's name either (Win32
# error 123, defect 252's measure on the Windows box), so `a\"b.h` is
# `unwritable_name` too, told before the thesis rule, and `check
# --permissive` refuses it as it refuses `*`; `'` and `//` stay C's.

extern "a'b.h"    #~ undefined_header_name
    function g1() -> i32

extern "a\"b.h"    #~ unwritable_name
    function g3() -> i32

extern "d//b.h"    #~ undefined_header_name
    function g4() -> i32

extern "e/*b.h"    #~ unwritable_name
    function g5() -> i32

extern "\tb.h"    #~ unshowable_name
    function g6() -> i32

function main()
    print(g1() + g3() + g4() + g5() + g6())
